# Android Best Practices

Before generating code

1. Understand the existing project.
2. Reuse existing architecture.
3. Avoid unnecessary refactoring.
4. Keep changes minimal.
5. Maintain coding consistency.

## Lifecycle

Use lifecycle-aware APIs.

Observe Flow using repeatOnLifecycle.

Cancel coroutines appropriately.

Clear View Binding in Fragments.

Never keep references to destroyed Activities or Fragments.

Before updating Fragment UI after asynchronous work, ensure:

- isAdded == true
- view != null
- binding != null

## Permissions

Handle runtime permissions correctly.

Support permission denial gracefully.

Support "Don't ask again".

## Compatibility

Generate code compatible with API 24–37.

Handle behaviour differences across Android versions.

Use AndroidX libraries.

Avoid deprecated APIs unless required for backward compatibility.

## Production Ready

Always consider

- configuration changes
- process death
- device reboot
- battery optimisation
- background execution limits
- exact alarm restrictions
- foreground service requirements
- notification permission (Android 13+)
- scoped storage
- lifecycle safety
- memory usage
- ANR prevention

Generate code that is maintainable, scalable, readable and production-ready.